+# Summary: range matching (`satisfies`, `max_satisfying`)
+
+## What changed
+- `depres/ranges.py`: implemented `satisfies(version, range_)` and `max_satisfying(versions, range_)` per `docs/RANGES.md`.
+  - Ranges are parsed into comparator sets (`||` unions, whitespace-joined comparators, hyphen ranges). Parsed ranges are cached.
+  - Partial versions, x-ranges, `~` and `^` are expanded into primitive `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `=` bounds.
+  - The prerelease rule is applied per comparator set.
+  - `max_satisfying` returns the original input string of the highest match, or `None`.
+- `tests/test_ranges_contract.py` (new): covers the examples in `docs/RANGES.md` (partials, operators, hyphen, tilde, caret, prerelease rule, unions, invalid inputs, `max_satisfying` return values).
+- No existing test was edited or deleted. `docs/`, `depres/version.py` and `depres/__init__.py` were not changed.
+
+## What I verified
+- `python -m unittest` (run in the project root): **Ran 21 tests, OK**. That is the 8 original tests in `tests/test_ranges.py` (previously 8 errors) plus 13 new contract tests. Before my change the same command gave `FAILED (errors=8)`.
+
+## Not verified / decisions to review
+- **`*` and `""` match prereleases.** The contract says these match "any version", so `satisfies("2.0.0-rc.1", "*")` is `True`. npm itself excludes prereleases for `*`. If CI or the lockfile checker expects npm behaviour, this needs changing.
+- **Partial versions with a prerelease are rejected** (e.g. `1.2-beta`). The contract doesn't cover this case, so I chose `ValueError`.
+- **Build metadata on partial versions is ignored** (e.g. `1.2+build` is accepted). The contract only says build metadata is ignored for comparison.
+- `satisfies` also accepts `Version` objects. A non-string, non-`Version` argument raises `TypeError`, not `ValueError`.
+- Only the Python 3 stdlib unittest suite was run. No other CI steps or lint were run, and I did not check the resolver's own callers.
+- `max_satisfying` returns the first occurrence when two inputs compare equal (e.g. they differ only in build metadata).
